---
import pivot from "../data/osint-pivot-map.json";
import tools from "../data/osint-tools.json";

const REPO = "https://github.com/iijarrett/personal-site";
---

<section class="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <h2 id="proof-title">Checked, not just claimed</h2>
  <ul class="rows">
    <li>
      <b>The numbers are counted.</b>{" "}{tools.toolCount} tools in {tools.sections.length} sections, {pivot.nodes.length}{" "}
      kinds of data and {pivot.edges.length} pivots, read from the guide's data when this site is built.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Every change is gated.</b> Type-check, lint, tests, the build and the built-output rules run
      on each pull request, and Lighthouse budgets are a required check before anything merges.{" "}
      <a href={`${REPO}/actions/workflows/ci.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the runs<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Scanned on a schedule.</b> CodeQL and the OpenSSF Scorecard run weekly.{" "}
      <a href={`${REPO}/actions/workflows/codeql.yml`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">CodeQL<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>,{" "}
      <a href="https://scorecard.dev/viewer/?uri=github.com/iijarrett/personal-site" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scorecard<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Releases are signed.</b> Each build carries a provenance and an SBOM attestation, and the
      deploy verifies both. <a href="/security/#release">How to check one yourself</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>The guide checks itself.</b> A weekly job in the guide's repository flags a tool that has
      moved, been renamed or gone quiet.{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/iijarrett/osint-field-guide/actions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Its runs<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
